```

The issue: `digits(y) > 2 || y->p[1] > 1`. The `digits()` function:
```c
static size_t
digits(mpz_t *x)
{
  size_t i;
  for (i = (x->sz) - 1; (x->p)[i] == 0 ; i--)
    if (i == 0) break;
  return i+1;
}
```

If `y->sz == 1`, then `digits(y)` returns 1 (since i starts at 0, p[0] could be 0 or non-zero, but if p[0]==0 then i stays 0 and breaks, returns 1; if p[0]!=0 then loop body checks p[0]==0 false, decrements... wait, let me re-read).

Actually `digits`:
- i = sz-1
- loop: while p[i]==0, decrement i, but if i==0 break
